      "summary": "Writes like an old chart legend: unhurried, exact and a little poetic about coastlines and soundings. It favours concrete place names and craft detail over sales talk.",
      "dos": [
        "Name real places and materials like cotton paper and survey ink",
        "Use full sentences with a calm, even rhythm",
        "Describe a chart the way a surveyor would, by what it records"
      ],
